---
import Layout from '../layouts/SimplePage.astro';
import CertificationBadge from '../components/CertificationBadge.astro';
import { certifications } from '../data/certifications';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="About Vaishakh G K"
>
	<center>
		<h1>I'm Vaishakh G K</h1>
		<p>
			Software engineer interested in how things work — and how they can be secured.
		</p>
	</center>

	<p>
		I'm a software engineer who enjoys building things, taking them apart,
		and understanding what happens underneath. My background is mainly in
		software and backend development, where I've worked on web applications,
		APIs, databases, distributed systems, and other networked software.
	</p>

	<p>
		Over time, that curiosity has led me deeper into cybersecurity. I'm
		interested in understanding how applications and systems can be
		analyzed, tested, and secured, and I'm currently exploring areas such
		as Linux, networking, application security, wireless security,
		low-level programming, and systems engineering.
	</p>

	<p>
		I enjoy learning by building. Some projects are useful applications,
		some are experiments, and some start simply because I wanted to know
		how something works. I work mostly with Go and C, while also spending
		a lot of time around Linux, networking, web technologies, and
		open-source software.
	</p>

	<h2>Beyond Programming</h2>

	<p>
		Computers aren't just something I use for work. I'm naturally curious
		about technology in general, so I often find myself exploring Linux,
		open-source projects, networking, hardware, embedded systems, and
		anything else that catches my attention.
	</p>

	<p>
		I enjoy experimenting with small ideas, building things that may never
		become finished projects, trying different tools, and occasionally
		going down a rabbit hole just to understand something that caught my
		attention.
	</p>

	<h2>Why I Have This Website</h2>

	<p>
		This website is more than a portfolio. It's my personal space on the
		internet — a place to keep track of what I'm building, what I'm
		learning, and the things I find interesting.
	</p>

	<p>
		I want to write about the things I learn in a way that is useful to
		other people. If I spend several hours figuring out something that
		seemed confusing at first, I'd rather document it so that someone
		else can understand it a little faster.
	</p>

	<p>
		You'll find my projects, technical notes, experiments, cybersecurity
		writing, and other things I'm interested in here. Some of them will
		be polished projects, while others will simply be a record of
		something I wanted to explore.
	</p>

	<p>
		This site will probably change as I do. The technologies I use,
		the things I work on, and even my interests will change over time.
		The idea is simply to keep building, keep learning, and share some
		of that journey along the way.
	</p>

    <center><h2>Certifications & Badges</h2></center>
	<div class="certification-badges">
		{certifications.map((cert) => (
			<CertificationBadge
				name={cert.name}
				issuer={cert.issuer}
				credlyUrl={cert.credlyUrl}
				dateIssued={cert.dateIssued}
				expirationDate={cert.expirationDate}
				inProgress={cert.inProgress}
				badgeImageUrl={cert.badgeImageUrl}
			/>
		))}
	</div>

	<style>
		.certification-badges {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
			max-width: 900px;
			margin: 2rem auto;
			gap: 1.5rem;
			justify-items: center;
		}

		@media (max-width: 767px) {
			.certification-badges {
				grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			}
		}
	</style>

</Layout>